    Sure, I can definitely help you with that. The structure of your paper largely depends on the type of research paper you are writing (expository, analytical, argumentative, etc.), but a common structure for a research paper includes an introduction, methods, results, and discussion sections. Here's a possible outline for your research paper on the impact of social media on mental health:

I. Introduction

* Background information on the issue
* Purpose and research questions
* Significance of the study

II. Literature Review

* Overview of previous research on social media and mental health
* Explanation of key concepts and definitions
* Discussion of the theoretical framework

III. Methods

* Description of the research design
* Participants and sample size
* Data collection and analysis methods

IV. Results

* Presentation of the findings
* Discussion of the results and their implications

V. Discussion

* Interpretation of the results
* Comparison with previous research
* Implications for future research and practice

VI. Conclusion

* Summary of the main findings
* Implications for social media use and mental health
* Limitations of the study
* Recommendations for future research

Remember, this is a general outline and you can adjust it according to your specific needs and requirements. Also, don't forget to cite your sources appropriately.

