One artist who comes to mind is Kehinde Wiley. He's a contemporary artist who uses traditional painting techniques to create contemporary portraits of people of color, often featuring them in poses reminiscent of classic European and American paintings. His work often challenges traditional ideas of beauty and portrays people who are often marginalized or overlooked.

Another artist who explores religious themes is Mark Bradford. His work often incorporates materials such as paint, fabric, and paper, and he often incorporates images from popular culture and the news into his pieces. His work often explores issues of race, class, and identity, and he uses art as a means of challenging preconceptions and sparking dialogue.

